Creating an Amazon RDS Database 
in this project we will create a MySQL database in a VPC 
MySQL is open source Relational Database Management System RDBMS .
1 - in the console search about RDS then choose Create a Database
Engine options : MySQL  
note : Aurora > MySQL in performance 
Templates : Dev/Test 
Availability and durability : Single DB instance 
2 - Settings
DB instance identifier : inventory-db
Master username : admin 
Credentials management : self managed 
Master password and Confirm master password : lab-password
3 - Instance Configuration 
DB instance class  : Burstable classes (includes t classes ) then select db.t3.micro 
4 - Storage section 
Storage type : General Purpose SSD (gp2) 
Allocated Storage : 20 G 
Expand Additional storage configuration 
Clear the option of ( enable storage Autoscaling)
5 - Connectivity 
VPC : Lab VPC learn how to make the VPC ( project 3) 
Choose existing security group  then choose App-SG  only 
note : create new security group if you don't have ( project 3 )
6 - Monitoring 
turn off Enable Enhanced monitoring 
7 - Additional configuration 
Initial database name: inventory
